        {
          "name": "account",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "FastDOL Delete Account",
              "id": "25c8d994-bb17-4f99-85ac-33381f58d8bc",
              "protocolProfileBehavior": {
                "disableBodyPruning": true
              },
              "request": {
                "method": "DELETE",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  },
                  {
                    "key": "Accept",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"password\": \"<string>\",\n  \"confirm\": \"<string>\"\n}",
                  "options": {
                    "raw": {
                      "headerFamily": "json",
                      "language": "json"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/dashboard/account",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "dashboard",
                    "account"
                  ]
                },
                "description": "Delete the authenticated customer's account and all associated data.\n\nImplements GDPR Article 17 (\"right to erasure\") and CCPA equivalents.\nRequires password re-authentication to prevent XSS / CSRF / session-theft\nescalating into full account wipe, plus an explicit \"DELETE\" confirmation\nstring to defeat accidental or malicious one-click destruction.\n\nCascades (via existing FKs in migrations/001_init + 002_add_constraints):\n  - api_keys, email_verifications, password_reset_tokens, subscriptions,\n    batch_jobs \u2014 ON DELETE CASCADE\n  - api_key_audit_log, api_usage \u2014 customer_id set to NULL (we keep the\n    audit/usage trail; the PII linkage is severed)\n  - audit_log \u2014 customer_id set to NULL (same rationale)\n\nNote: the customers table still carries a vestigial `stripe_customer_id`\ncolumn from when paid tiers were self-serve via Stripe. The column is\nnot selected here \u2014 Stripe was retired in the May 2026 redesign and\ncommercial accounts are now handled out-of-band. If we ever need the\nhistorical mapping back, it's still in the DB row; we just don't surface\nit from this delete flow."
              },
              "response": [
                {
                  "id": "0614d091-f2a8-4016-8183-27c96826bed0",
                  "name": "Successful Response",
                  "originalRequest": {
                    "method": "DELETE",
                    "header": [
                      {
                        "key": "Content-Type",
                        "value": "application/json"
                      },
                      {
                        "key": "Accept",
                        "value": "application/json"
                      }
                    ],
                    "body": {
                      "mode": "raw",
                      "raw": "{\n  \"password\": \"<string>\",\n  \"confirm\": \"<string>\"\n}",
                      "options": {
                        "raw": {
                          "headerFamily": "json",
                          "language": "json"
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "url": {
                      "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/dashboard/account",
                      "host": [
                        "{{baseUrl}}"
                      ],
                      "path": [
                        "dashboard",
                        "account"
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  "status": "OK",
                  "code": 200,
                  "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
                  "header": [
